This product bundles third-party syntax-highlighting grammars (via the
`two-face` crate) under their own permissive licenses. Those licenses are
reproduced in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The local voices (Kokoro, and the studio voice built on Qwen3-TTS) are not
bundled. At the user's request Redline downloads them, with a private Python
runtime, into its app data folder, and runs them as separate processes. What
is downloaded, and under which licenses, is listed in VOICE_ENGINE_NOTICES.md.
This includes the GCC runtime libraries and libquadmath that scipy's macOS
wheel ships.
